[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5327645174","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411#issuecomment-5327645174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411","id":5327645174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks8AAAABPY1p9g","user":{"login":"mengcar","id":203223903,"node_id":"U_kgDODBzzXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203223903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar","html_url":"https://github.com/mengcar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mengcar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T11:40:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T11:40:51Z","body":"I measured the `k8s.io/kubernetes` surface of `pkg/scheduler` with `go list` while looking at #141403 (before realising PR was already open for it, whoops haha) but this did lead to some questions:\n\nI totalled 10 problematic packages, matching the allow-list in #141415. 5 are covered by existing issues described in this issue's description and the ktesting note covers 2 more. So that leaves 3 I can't account for:\n\n- `pkg/controller` in `volumebinding/binder_test.go`\n- `pkg/controller/volume/persistentvolume/testing` in `volumebinding/binder_test.go`\n- `test/utils/image` in `pkg/scheduler/testing/wrappers.go`\n\nBoth `pkg/controller` entries come from that one test file, but they're very different in weight. `controller.NoResyncPeriodFunc` is 3 lines and seems trivially inlineable, but`pvtesting.VolumeReactor` is more like 500+ lines and simulating PV controller behaviour, which is much more complex. Is the intent to restructure that test, or does the reactor need a home outside k/k?\n\n`test/utils/image` enters through `wrappers.go`, which calls `imageutils.GetPauseImageName()` in five places to set a container image on pod fixtures. That pulls in the e2e image registry machinery for what seems to be one image string. `pkg/scheduler/testing` has 50 consuming packages in tree, so I assume it moves to staging too? As far as I can tell, nothing ever actually pulls these images (unit tests use fake caches, integration runs no kubelet), so a plain const would probably do, but are there any cases I am missing?\n  \nAs mentioned in #141410 this is my first contribution into k/k so thank your for your patience :-) - I would like to get involved in this issue so happy to file and take any of these. If there are any other good entry issues you are aware of please also let me know.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5327645174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5327814909","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411#issuecomment-5327814909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411","id":5327814909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks8AAAABPZAA_Q","user":{"login":"antekjb","id":3142207,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDIyMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3142207?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb","html_url":"https://github.com/antekjb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antekjb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T11:56:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T11:56:13Z","body":"Thank you for checking dependencies,\n1. ```pvtesting.VolumeReactor``` maybe we can move this function to ```k8s.io/component-helpers/storage/volume/testing``` \n2. ```controller.NoResyncPeriodFunc``` sounds like candidate for inlining/making a copy, or just change it to 0 and add comment, as ```NoResyncPeriodFunc``` is always returning 0\n3. From ```test/utils/image``` we are using only ```imageutils.GetPauseImageName()``` so we should be able to add const/inline function \n\n @brejman WDYT?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5327814909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5329460798","html_url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411#issuecomment-5329460798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/141411","id":5329460798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAToIks8AAAABPakePg","user":{"login":"brejman","id":9309441,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzMDk0NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9309441?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman","html_url":"https://github.com/brejman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brejman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-18T14:16:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T08:09:42Z","body":"1. It looks like we're using `pvtesting.VolumeReactor` only to check how the code behaves in case of API error (by setting up a version conflict). The test could be simplified if we used fake.Clientset.PrependReactor() to mock errors directly instead. If such refactor turns out to be too complex, moving the test helper to `k8s.io/component-helpers/storage/volume/testing` seems reasonable as well.\n\n2. Agreed. For `imageutils.GetPauseImageName()`, some places define simply `\"pause\"` string instead, we can follow the same pattern: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/c44d2a82ef7f87c8b4278cd13af0a55614ed2a53/pkg/scheduler/testing/wrappers.go#L517 As you noticed, it shouldn't really matter what goes there.\n\n3. Agreed. `NoResyncPeriodFunc` is already duplicated in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/c44d2a82ef7f87c8b4278cd13af0a55614ed2a53/staging/src/k8s.io/sample-controller/controller_test.go#L46","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/comments/5329460798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,